; Exercise 08-parse-date (chapter 8).
;
; (parse-date text) reads a date written YEAR-MONTH-DAY, such as
; "2026-11-15", and returns a result:
;   (:ok {:year 2026 :month 11 :day 15})
; or the first failure among these, checked in this order:
;   (:error "expected YEAR-MONTH-DAY" text)   not three parts around "-"
;   (:error "not a number" part)              a part that is not an Integer
;   (:error "month out of range" month)       a month outside 1 to 12
;   (:error "day out of range" day)           a day outside the month
;
; Write a helper that reads one part as a result, and put the steps
; together with (chain then …). days-in-month, from the library time,
; gives the days of a month: (days-in-month 2024 2) is 29.
; Then run: tutorial/check.sh 08-parse-date

